    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0582" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/2351: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Arica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Von
                            Tresckow</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-05-27T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1926—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Lassiter. Your telegram May 26, 10 p.m. Please continue to send in reports as
                    detailed as possible covering all incidents such as you have reported. Mr.
                    Stimson and Mr. Dennis<anchor n="3" xml:id="d300-f1"/> are working continuously
                    on this matter; early next week they expect to be able to make a complete report
                    based on all data available here. We all appreciate fully the difficulties and
                    embarrassments of your position as well as the dangers which are inherent in the
                    local situation and at earliest possible moment I shall give you decisions on
                    policy. Please rest assured that all phases of the problem are receiving most
                    earnest and active attention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d300-f1" n="3" xml:id="d300-f1-content">
                <p>William C. Dennis, formerly at Arica as general legal adviser to the president of
                    the Plebiscitary Commission.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
